index f5f3604b..ee968243 100644
--- a/packages/portable/GPU-SPEC.md
+++ b/packages/portable/GPU-SPEC.md
@@ -25,6 +25,15 @@ The committed portable CPU implementation and its public TypeScript APIs remain
 - MP4 remuxing uses the HEVC elementary demuxer and `hvc1` sample entry. Before atomic publication, decoded codec, dimensions, full frame count and rational cadence must match the request. Tests verify decoded limited BT.709 color, HEVC Main profile, range, both transports, callbacks and refusal of mismatched helper receipts.
 - Qualification uses separate source/helper/runtime pins, direct NV12 references, every decoded frame and unchanged quality floors. Small scene qualification is not a full 4K comparison or speed claim; the comparison owner retains its harness and historical clocks.
 
+## MoltenVK backend acceptance
+
+- Explicit `backend: 'vulkan'` on macOS arm64 selects a separately built Skia Vulkan helper with pinned public-API MoltenVK. Omitted backend preserves Metal; unknown backends, unavailable runtime or unsupported platforms reject without raster/encoder fallback. Linux Vulkan Video and Windows remain separate unsupported hardware cells.
+- Require an integrated/discrete Vulkan device, graphics queue, `VK_EXT_metal_objects`, portability subset and exact imported/exported Metal texture identity. The Vulkan and retained encoder texture must belong to the same actual Metal GPU. Private raw pixels never pass through JavaScript, a pipe or application CPU conversion in the hardware lane.
+- Actual Skia Vulkan submission precedes a bounded Vulkan fence wait; that completion precedes the retained GPU BT.709 NV12 conversion and hardware VideoToolbox submission. Imported images/device and source texture remain owned until all use finishes; errors drain before releasing resources. Pool/GOP/bitrate/font/Canvas/atomic-publication bounds remain unchanged.
+- Vulkan JSON protocol8/binary9 receipts bind backend, Skia Vulkan rasterizer, MoltenVK Metal-object interop, shared texture, codec and actual required hardware. A Metal receipt or software/unshared bridge rejects before publication. Commands remain HGF5. Both H.264 and HEVC use the retained compressed packet extraction.
+- Runtime installation is optional and checksum pinned, bounded and atomic. Existing different runtime installations are preserved and rejected. The runtime is a local build artifact, never scene input or an implicit global installation.
+- Independent direct NV12/lossless references, decoded every-frame quality/cadence/color, actual GPU/transfer probes and positive/negative controls are required before any performance conclusion. Three setup frames do not qualify the full4K workload or total zero-copy. Vulkan trace sidecar `<trace>.vulkan.jsonl` binds sharing and fence events separately from retained converter/encoder traces.
+
 ## Bounded encoder overlap acceptance
 
 ### Bounded bitrate controls
